PURPOSE of kernel/general/include

A case for storing helper tools. At first, Kabi and Kmod both need a tool
for getting kernel and kernel-debuginfo of a specified version. The tool
was stored in general/kabi, but in kmod tests, I also need it, so have to
move that tool to a upper dir.

So start from this, I add this include dir to store some scripts or helper
functions for kernel general testing.

Tools & scraipts
  1) wget-kernel.sh
     sh wget-kernel.sh --nvr 4.5.0-0.48.el7 --arch aarch64 --debug (debuginfo)
     sh wget-kernel.sh --nvr 4.5.0-0.48.el7 --arch x86_64 (kernel)
     sh wget-kernel.sh --nvr 4.5.0-0.48.el7 --arch x86_64 --fw (firmware)

